{"chunk_id": "46f42ac58edf", "text": "This section links the power of Brahmanical spiritual authority with divine warfare and culminates in Bhishma\u2019s theological praise of Krishna. The narrative begins with Vedic mantras destroying the Kapas; although the gods defeat the Danavas in battle, Narada reveals that the real victory was achieved through the energy of Brahmanas. Arjuna affirms his lifelong devotion to Brahmanas and attributes his own power to the grace of Dattatreya, while the wind-god instructs him to protect them as a sacred Kshatriya duty and warns of a future danger from the Bhrigu race. In the following dialogue, Bhishma\u2014aware that death is near\u2014directs Yudhishthira to Krishna for ultimate answers and delivers a sweeping declaration of Krishna\u2019s cosmic identity as creator, sustainer, and restorer of righteousness. The passage emphasizes the hierarchy of spiritual power and Krishna\u2019s supreme, all-encompassing divinity.\nBhishma, nearing death, tells Yudhishthira that Krishna embodies the cosmic creator and sustainer, urging him to learn remaining dharma from Krishna.\nThemes: divinity of Krishna, dharma and social order, cosmic creation, Bhishma's approaching death, praise of Brahmanas", "vector": [-0.000613454554695636, -0.014765988104045391, -0.00178113067522645, 0.006266266573220491, -0.0027321716770529747, 0.010875667445361614, -0.01973658613860607, -0.013473632745444775, -0.010418372228741646, -0.018464112654328346, 0.005215813405811787, -0.0002903657150454819, -0.0005248122615739703, 0.003403202397748828, -0.0012327081058174372, -0.00233618076890707, 0.042018115520477295, -0.018371328711509705, 0.02084999904036522, -0.01427555549889803, 0.0025250634644180536, -0.007489033509045839, 0.0001556418283144012, 0.01674097217619419, -0.010186410509049892, 0.012897043488919735, 0.015256419777870178, -0.030062172561883926, 0.004278027452528477, -0.01888827048242092, -0.0023759454488754272, -0.010736490599811077, -0.0007406190270558,